IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `jccv-party`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1993 (ACT) -- worked cases, from the seat of the party to a civil proceeding.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (A1993-60, R4), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act; the
-- facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every opinion of a court is given as a fact.
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS on the stable l4, so the regulative rule is asserted through
-- CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED, and the breach is also #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line.

-- Short names for the courts, for readability only.
GIVETH A `Court`
`ACT SC` MEANS `the ACT Supreme Court`
GIVETH A `Court`
`FedC` MEANS `the Federal Court of Australia`
GIVETH A `Court`
`FamC` MEANS `the Family Court (the Family Court of Australia, now the FCFCOA Division 1)`
GIVETH A `Court`
`NSW SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of another State (one of the six States, or the Northern Territory)`
GIVETH A `Court`
`Norfolk SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of an external Territory`
GIVETH A `Court`
`WA FamC` MEANS `the Family Court of Western Australia (a State Family Court)`
GIVETH A `Court`
`ACT lower` MEANS `another ACT court, or a tribunal established under an ACT Act`
GIVETH A `Court`
`other court` MEANS `another court or tribunal`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 4. HYPOTHETICAL: Mei is hurt in a fall at a Canberra shopping centre and lives in Sydney. Her negligence claim is an ACT
-- matter (the ACT Supreme Court has jurisdiction under ACT law alone).
-- Filed in the NSW Supreme Court: s 4(3).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `NSW SC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(3))`
-- Filed in the Federal Court: s 4(1).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `FedC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Federal Court has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(1))`
-- The Family Court: s 4(2).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `FamC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Family Court has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(2))`
-- The Family Court of WA: s 4(4) (s 3 keeps it out of s 4(3)).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `WA FamC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the State Family Court of another State has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(4))`
-- Norfolk Island's Supreme Court is "the Supreme Court ... of a Territory": s 4(3).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `Norfolk SC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(3))`
-- An ACT matter by removal under s 8 (paragraph (b) of the definition), not by the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `FedC` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Federal Court has original and appellate jurisdiction in ACT matters (s 4(1))`
-- Not an ACT matter (say a claim the ACT Supreme Court has only under a Commonwealth law): s 4 gives nothing.
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `NSW SC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the matter is not an ACT matter, so section 4 of this Act gives the court nothing (the Commonwealth's or another State's cross-vesting law may)`
-- Criminal: s 4(5).
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `NSW SC` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: section 4 gives no court jurisdiction in criminal matters (s 4(5))`
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `FedC` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: section 4 gives no court jurisdiction in criminal matters (s 4(5))`
-- The ACT Supreme Court itself: this Act gives it nothing by s 4; s 9.
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `ACT SC` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `this Act gives the ACT Supreme Court nothing here: an ACT matter is by definition within its own jurisdiction, and s 9 lets it exercise whatever jurisdiction the Commonwealth's or another State's cross-vesting law gives it`
-- A lower court: not covered.
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `ACT lower` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`
#ASSERT `Can this court hear my ACT matter question` `other court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5. HYPOTHETICAL: Mei sues in the ACT Supreme Court; the shopping centre's owner has already sued its cleaning contractor
-- in the NSW Supreme Court over the same fall.
-- Ground (i) appears: s 5(2).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `NSW SC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
-- Only ground (ii): s 5(2).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `NSW SC` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
-- Only ground (iii): s 5(2).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `NSW SC` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
-- No ground appears.
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `NSW SC` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: none of the grounds in section 5 appears to the court, so section 5 does not require a transfer`
-- The ACT Supreme Court to the Family Court of WA (a "Supreme Court of another State" by s 3): s 5(2).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `WA FamC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
-- The ACT Supreme Court to the Federal Court: s 5(1).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `FedC` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court, as the case may be (s 5(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `FamC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court, as the case may be (s 5(1))`
-- s 6A applies: s 5(1) does not require it, whatever appears (s 6A(4)).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `FedC` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `not required: section 6A applies, so section 5(1) does not require the ACT Supreme Court to transfer my federal matter proceeding; it may still transfer it if it considers that appropriate (s 6A(4), (5))`
-- s 6A does not touch s 5(2).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT SC` `NSW SC` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
-- The NSW Supreme Court to the ACT Supreme Court: s 5(3).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `NSW SC` `ACT SC` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: that other Supreme Court must transfer it to the ACT Supreme Court (s 5(3))`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `Norfolk SC` `ACT SC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: that other Supreme Court must transfer it to the ACT Supreme Court (s 5(3))`
-- The Federal Court to the ACT Supreme Court: s 5(4).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `ACT SC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the ACT Supreme Court (s 5(4))`
-- ... unless s 6A applies (s 6A(3)).
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `ACT SC` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `not required: section 6A applies, so section 5(4) does not apply; the Federal Court or the Family Court may transfer my proceeding to the ACT Supreme Court if it considers that appropriate (s 6A(2), (3))`
-- Between the Federal Court and the Family Court: s 5(5); ground (iii) (there (ii)) works.
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `FamC` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the court must transfer it to the other of the Federal Court and the Family Court (s 5(5))`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FamC` `FedC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the court must transfer it to the other of the Federal Court and the Family Court (s 5(5))`
-- s 5(5) has no "having regard to" ground: the weighing alone does not require a transfer.
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `FamC` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: none of the grounds in section 5 appears to the court, so section 5 does not require a transfer`
-- Pairs no subsection joins: the NSW Supreme Court to the Federal Court (that is the Commonwealth Act's and NSW's business),
-- the Federal Court to the NSW Supreme Court, the same court twice, a lower ACT court.
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `NSW SC` `FedC` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `NSW SC` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `FedC` `FedC` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `ACT lower` `ACT SC` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`
-- Between the Supreme Courts of two other States: not this Act's pair.
#ASSERT `Must my proceeding be transferred question` `NSW SC` `WA FamC` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`

-- s 5(6): Mei's claim went to NSW; her separate claim against the cleaning contractor is still in the ACT Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `Must my related proceeding follow question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer my related proceeding to the court it sent the first proceeding to (s 5(6))`
#ASSERT `Must my related proceeding follow question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 5(6) requires the related proceeding to follow only if the court considers it related and that the interests of justice call for it`
#ASSERT `Must my related proceeding follow question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 5(6) requires the related proceeding to follow only if the court considers it related and that the interests of justice call for it`
#ASSERT `Must my related proceeding follow question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 5(6) applies only once the court has transferred another proceeding under a cross-vesting law`

-- s 5(7): a party (or intervener) may apply; a stranger is not covered.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a transfer question` TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: as a party I may apply for a transfer under section 5; the court may also act of its own initiative, and an Attorney-General may apply (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a transfer question` FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the person is not a party to the proceeding (a party includes an intervener); this Act gives a non-party no application`

-- s 5(8): Mei's Canberra lawyer follows her claim to Sydney.
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer keep acting question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: my lawyer has the same right to practise in the new court, for my transferred proceeding and any related proceeding to be decided with it, as in a federal court exercising federal jurisdiction (s 5(8))`
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer keep acting question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 5(8) gives that right only to a lawyer entitled to practise in the court the proceeding came from`
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer keep acting question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 5(8) covers only the transferred proceeding and a related one to be decided together with it`
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer keep acting question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 5(8) applies only to a proceeding transferred under a cross-vesting law`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 6. HYPOTHETICAL: Daniel, an injured worker, challenges in the ACT Supreme Court a Commonwealth decision under the ADJR Act.
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(c) the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(a) Part IV of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (restrictive trade practices)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(b) questions of law on appeal from, or referred or stated by, a Commonwealth tribunal, body or office-holder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(e) the Federal Court's original jurisdiction under section 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
-- (ab): to the family court the Supreme Court thinks appropriate.
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(ab) section 60G of the Family Law Act 1975 (leave for a prescribed adoption)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to whichever of the Family Court, the Family Court of Western Australia or the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory it thinks appropriate (s 6(1), (2)(b))`
-- (aa): the gap in s 6(2) (NOTES.md finding 3).
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(aa) the Competition Code of the ACT or the Northern Territory` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but the text names no receiving court: the matter is a special federal matter under paragraph (aa), which s 6(2) does not mention (s 6(1))`
-- A s 6(3) order keeps it.
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(c) the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the ACT Supreme Court has ordered, for special reasons, that it determine the proceeding itself (s 6(3)); it can do so only after notice to both Attorneys-General and a reasonable time (s 6(4))`
-- s 6A applies to an ADJR matter: not required (s 6A(4)).
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(c) the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not required: section 6A applies, so section 6 does not require the ACT Supreme Court to transfer my federal matter proceeding; it may still do so if it considers that appropriate (s 6A(4), (5))`
-- s 6A cannot apply to a paragraph (a) matter, so the input changes nothing.
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `(a) Part IV of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (restrictive trade practices)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `ACT SC` `not a special federal matter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the matter is not a special federal matter`
#ASSERT `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court question` `NSW SC` `(c) the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 6 applies only to a proceeding pending in the ACT Supreme Court`

-- s 6(4), (5)(b): the regulative rule. The court gives Daniel 14 days to notify both Attorneys-General.
-- Notice on day 14, the last day; the Supreme Court then orders that it keep the proceeding: fulfilled.
`notice on the last day, then the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6(5)(b) -- I must give the notice the court directed` 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the party the court directed` `give written notice of the nature of the special federal matter to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and the Attorney-General of the ACT` 14), (EVENT `the ACT Supreme Court` `order that the proceeding be determined by the ACT Supreme Court` 40))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `notice on the last day, then the order` EQUALS TRUE
-- Notice on day 1: fulfilled once the order follows.
`notice early, then the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6(5)(b) -- I must give the notice the court directed` 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the party the court directed` `give written notice of the nature of the special federal matter to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and the Attorney-General of the ACT` 1), (EVENT `the ACT Supreme Court` `order that the proceeding be determined by the ACT Supreme Court` 30))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `notice early, then the order` EQUALS TRUE
-- Notice on day 15, one day late: breached, so not fulfilled.
`notice one day late` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6(5)(b) -- I must give the notice the court directed` 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the party the court directed` `give written notice of the nature of the special federal matter to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and the Attorney-General of the ACT` 15))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `notice one day late` EQUALS FALSE
#TRACE `s 6(5)(b) -- I must give the notice the court directed` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the party the court directed` DOES `give written notice of the nature of the special federal matter to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and the Attorney-General of the ACT` AT 15
-- expect: BREACH by the party the court directed, "s 6(5)(b): ... did not give it in the time the court allowed"

-- The seat question on the notice.
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Attorneys-General question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court has directed me to give written notice of the nature of the special federal matter to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and the Attorney-General of the ACT, in the time it allowed (s 6(4)(a), (5)(b))`
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Attorneys-General question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not unless the court directs me: the Act names no one who must give the notice, but the court cannot keep the matter until it is satisfied the notice was given and a reasonable time has passed (s 6(4))`
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Attorneys-General question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the notice is needed only where a special federal matter is pending in the ACT Supreme Court and it is asked to keep it (s 6(3), (4))`

-- s 6(5)(a): adjournment costs.
#ASSERT `Can my adjournment costs be dealt with question` TRUE EQUALS `possibly: the ACT Supreme Court may make such order as to the costs of the adjournment as it thinks fit (s 6(5)(a)); it is a discretion`
#ASSERT `Can my adjournment costs be dealt with question` FALSE EQUALS `no: section 6(5)(a) deals only with the costs of an adjournment for the notice to the Attorneys-General`

-- s 6(7): urgent interim relief.
#ASSERT `Can I still get urgent interim relief question` TRUE EQUALS `yes: section 6 does not stop the ACT Supreme Court granting me urgent interlocutory relief, as the court thinks the interests of justice require (s 6(7))`
#ASSERT `Can I still get urgent interim relief question` FALSE EQUALS `section 6 does not stand in the way, but the ACT Supreme Court has not found that the interests of justice call for urgent interlocutory relief (s 6(7))`

-- ss 6(8), 7(7): decisions not invalidated.
#ASSERT `Is the decision invalid question` `the ACT Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without a s 6(3) order or without the s 6(4) notice` TRUE EQUALS `answered` `no: nothing in section 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `Is the decision invalid question` `the ACT Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without a s 6(3) order or without the s 6(4) notice` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `section 6(8) does not save it: it saves only a decision given through inadvertence; this Act does not say whether the decision is otherwise invalid`
#ASSERT `Is the decision invalid question` `the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a federal Full Court or the High Court (through inadvertence, or because the interests of justice required it to proceed)` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: nothing in section 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `Is the decision invalid question` `something else` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `this Act says nothing of that decision`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 6A. HYPOTHETICAL: Ana seeks ADJR review of a Commonwealth officer's decision made under an ACT Act of the kind in
-- paragraph (ca) of the ADJR Act's definition; her related claim under that ACT Act is in the ACT Magistrates Court.
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `FedC` EQUALS `answered` `section 6A applies: the Federal Court or the Family Court may transfer my proceeding to the ACT Supreme Court if it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice (including having related proceedings heard together); s 5(4) does not apply (s 6A(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ACT SC` EQUALS `answered` `section 6A applies: sections 5(1) and 6 do not require the ACT Supreme Court to transfer my proceeding to the Federal Court or the Family Court, but it may do so if it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice (s 6A(4), (5))`
-- Each of the four conditions failing on its own.
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `FedC` EQUALS `answered` `no: section 6A does not apply to my proceeding (s 6A(1))`
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `FedC` EQUALS `answered` `no: section 6A does not apply to my proceeding (s 6A(1))`
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `FedC` EQUALS `answered` `no: section 6A does not apply to my proceeding (s 6A(1))`
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `ACT SC` EQUALS `answered` `no: section 6A does not apply to my proceeding (s 6A(1))`
-- In the NSW Supreme Court: s 6A says nothing.
#ASSERT `What section 6A does for me question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `NSW SC` EQUALS `not covered` `this provision of the Act does not speak to a proceeding in that court, or to that pair of courts`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 7. HYPOTHETICAL: Mei loses before a single judge of the ACT Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a single judge of the ACT Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `to the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court only (s 7(3))`
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a single judge of the ACT Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court; not to the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court (s 7(4))`
-- A Schedule matter mixed with another: s 7(4) still (s 7(5) is about a State Family Court judge only).
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a single judge of the ACT Supreme Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court; not to the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court (s 7(4))`
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `not to the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court (s 7(1)), and not to the other of the Federal Court and the Family Court (s 7(2)); this Act does not say where it does lie`
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a single judge of the Family Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `not to the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court (s 7(1)), and not to the other of the Federal Court and the Family Court (s 7(2)); this Act does not say where it does lie`
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a judge of the Family Court of Western Australia` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `the appeal may be dealt with as if no matter in it arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(5)); this Act does not otherwise say where it lies`
-- s 7(5) needs both kinds of matter.
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of a judge of the Family Court of Western Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this Act does not say where this appeal lies: that is for the Act that created the court`
#ASSERT `Where must I appeal question` `a decision of another court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `this Act does not say where this appeal lies: that is for the Act that created the court`

-- s 7(6): the appeal has begun in the Full Court.
#ASSERT `What happens to my appeal question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court must transfer my appeal to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires (s 7(6))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my appeal question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Full Court of the ACT Supreme Court may go on to decide my appeal, because the interests of justice require it; its decision is not invalid for that (s 7(6), (7)(a))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my appeal question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `section 7(6) does not apply: my appeal is not one that section 7(4) sends to a federal Full Court`

